2026-10-31T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Bao runs three replicas on the FDB machines
 # uuid: 22a44957-cbde-5229-854c-e9beb840aede
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-31T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2353) 'weftspun-bao and the weftspun-fdb machines it runs on.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Bao runs as three replicas, one beside each FDB machine.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Bao was one machine, and every consumer now depends on it: every routine credential read, coordination write and policy check routes through Bao, so one outage stops them all.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Deploy the image to the three weftspun-fdb machines one at a time and unseal each, then destroy the `weftspun-bao` app once the three serve.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Bao runs three replicas on the FDB machines
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2353) '`ha_enabled = true`, coordinated over FDB (operator, 2026-10-13). The `weftspun-bao` app retires once the three instances serve. Superseded on 2026-11-01: Bao runs as one instance beside a single-node FDB cluster on one Fly machine, restored from the R2 backup, with `ha_enabled = false` (operator, 2026-11-01).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2353) 'RFD66606-2140, RFD66606-2144, RFD66606-2145, RFD66606-2146. Split from the old RFD66606-2147: RFD66606-2354 (unseal), 2355 (cache), 2356 (no CDN proxy).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Why HA now, not before
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2353) 'RFD66606-2140 chose `ha_enabled = "false"` when Bao was one machine and one operator. Under that arrangement, Bao being down meant one thing was down: the Bao API. Everything else routed around Bao by holding its credentials in Fly secrets or 1P.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2353) 'RFD66606-2146 turned that inside out. Every consumer now authenticates to Bao with its per-service cert, reads its credentials from Bao at runtime, and coordinates state through Bao's KV. When Bao goes down, the DNS-editing path goes down, the R2-write path goes down, the FDB coordinator info lookup goes down, and any new spend gate that follows the same pattern goes down with them. The single-machine posture that was fine as a convenience store is not fine as the switchboard.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Colocated on the FDB machines
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2353) 'The operator chose on 2026-10-13 to run Bao on the three weftspun-fdb machines instead of in its own app. The Fly plan in use includes three `shared-cpu-1x` 256 MB machines and 3 GB of volumes; three FDB machines plus a separate Bao machine overran both, and the separate machine bought no redundancy. FDB keeps `double` redundancy and three coordinators, so one machine may still be lost.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Each machine runs fdbserver, the backup agent, Bao, tailscaled and sshd, at 512 MB. Measured on 2026-10-13 at 256 MB: an FDB machine used about 130 MB, and the Bao machine about 130 MB, of which Bao was 77 MB, tailscaled 26 MB and the plugin 18 MB. The two together do not fit in the 207 MB a 256 MB machine leaves usable.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2353) '- The `weftspun-bao` app retires once the three instances serve. Its volume held no secrets: Bao's storage is FDB, and the volume kept the tailnet identity, the SSH host key and renewed listener certificates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2353) '- Each instance advertises its own machine address as `api_addr` and `cluster_addr`, so standbys forward to the active instance. Standbys forward every read to the active instance.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2353) '- Clients keep verifying the listener as `weftspun-bao.internal`; the name in the certificate does not move with the app.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2353) '- One machine carries the existing tailnet state and keeps the `weftspun-bao` node; the others join under their own names.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2353) '- The SSH tunnel port is balanced across all three machines, so they share one host key, held as a secret rather than generated per volume.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2353) '- The change is proved on a throwaway three-machine app before weftspun-fdb is touched: an initialised test Bao, a secret written and read back, one machine restarted and unsealed while the others keep serving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Replicas: 3 in sjc, coordinated over FDB
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2353) 'OpenBao's FDB backend supports HA by leader election over the same storage the writes go to. One instance runs on each FDB machine, so Bao spreads across the same three zones FDB does.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Standby replicas can either serve reads directly or forward every request to the leader. Read-serving standbys would suit the read/write ratio the cert-auth path establishes (many reads per one write); until the fork is shown to serve reads from a standby, standbys forward.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2353) 'The 3-machine scale exposes one wrinkle: three machines mean three seal states, three unseal calls per fleet restart. This is the reason auto-unseal stays the goal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Migration path
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Enabling the replicas on the live cluster is:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2353) '1. Update `service-openbao/config-fdb.hcl`: `ha_enabled = "true"`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2353) '2. Build one image carrying the FDB server and Bao, and deploy it to the three weftspun-fdb machines one at a time, unsealing each.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2353) '3. Stop the `weftspun-bao` app, then destroy it once the three serve.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2353) 'A desk reaches the active instance
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Read on 2026-10-16. The three instances elect one leader, and only the leader answers a login; a standby redirects to the leader's `<machine>.vm.weftspun-fdb.internal` address, which no desk resolves. Two of the three carried tailnet names that day (`weftspun-bao-3`, `weftspun-bao-4`), both unsealed standbys, and the leader, the third machine, had none, so a desk asking the tailnet found no leader and the desk helper exited without a word.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2353) 'The route that worked: read `sys/leader` from any instance (no token, mTLS only), take the machine id out of `leader_address`, and run `fly proxy 8200:8200 <id>.vm.weftspun-fdb.internal -a weftspun-fdb` as a background process. The desk then uses `BAO_ADDR=https://127.0.0.1:8200` with `BAO_TLS_SERVER_NAME=weftspun-bao.internal` and its agent certificate. The proxy exits on its own after some minutes; a `connection refused` on 127.0.0.1:8200 means restart it, not that Bao is down.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2353) 'The retired `weftspun-bao` app still exists, stopped. `fly proxy -a weftspun-bao` fails with `host was not found in DNS` because nothing runs there, and starting its machine brings up a second Bao against the same FDB storage, which stops again within a minute. It was started twice that day by mistake before the route above was found; it is not started again, and its deletion is an open item.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Sub-decisions open
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2353) '- Delete the retired `weftspun-bao` app and its volume, so a desk cannot start a second Bao by mistake.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2353) '- Every instance joins the tailnet under its own name, or the leader's name is published where a desk can read it without a Fly login.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2353) '- 3 replicas, one per FDB machine (operator, 2026-10-13).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2353) '- Standbys serve reads (`disable_performance_standby = false`) vs forward to leader. Read-heavy workload argues for serving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2353) '- The FDB and Bao data machines run as one machine or as an HA set; the one-machine form relies on tested backups (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2353) 'Sources
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2353) '- OpenBao HA storage docs (FDB backend supports HA via leader election on the shared FDB cluster).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2353) '- RFD66606-2140 (Bao on FDB, this raises its ambition), 2145 (leaf and CA rotation cadence this HA has to survive), 2146 (the capability topology this now underwrites).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2353) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2353) 'RFD66606-2140's `ha_enabled = "false"` fit that framing. RFD66606-2146 then moved every routine credential read, coordination write, and policy check onto Bao. Every consumer now depends on Bao being up, and RFD66606-2140's reliability budget is smaller than what routes through Bao now needs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2353  1 LINE
 Text:Written

